    "narrative": "The primary focal point for LawDog today is **Lawrence Butler**, who commands our highest efficiency score of 73.46. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Bassitt, pairing a positive park factor with a significant platoon advantage that amplifies his upside in the 4-hole. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple at 72.96; while his score takes a slight dip due to the risk of an elite hold pitcher suppressing stolen base opportunities, his placement in the 3-spot against Lugo provides high-floor production that is essential for our weekly Roto standings. **Cal Raleigh** rounds out our top-tier starters at 70.73, buoyed by a substantial +19% SP skill adjustment against Scherzer, whose current metrics offer a prime environment for power production.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles regarding our depth. **Gleyber Torres** is our most concerning start, sliding into the lineup with a marginal 40.18 score; his value is heavily compressed by a brutal matchup against Glasnow, and he only maintains his spot due to the scarcity of high-speed options on our bench. **Yainer Diaz** and **Daulton Varsho** are buoyed by wind-aided projections, though both are battling platoon-related efficiency drops against Thornton. Regarding the bench, **Justin Crawford** remains our most critical \"near-miss\"; his elite sprint speed makes him the first man up if we need to aggressively chase stolen base volume, but he is currently excluded due to the lack of a verified path to plate appearances in today's active rotation.\n\nRisk management is paramount today given the high concentration of tough matchups. We have moved to protect game caps by keeping **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman** on the IL, alongside minor league assignments for **Tyler Freeman**. Monitor the status of **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland**, as any shifts in daily lineup availability could force a pivot if our current outfield configuration underperforms against the likes of Imanaga or Kikuchi. Keep a close eye on **Bryce Harper**, who carries a strong 67.09 projection; his xwOBA remains elite, and he represents our best chance at neutralizing the risk posed by Kikuchi\u2019s arm.",
